      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "If $u+\\frac{v}{2}=1,$ then $u=$",
      "worked_solution": "We need to isolate the variable $u.$ To do this, we treat $v$ as though it were a constant and apply the addition and multiplication principles as usual.\n\nIn this case, we simply subtract $\\frac{v}{2}$ from both sides of the equation: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u+\\frac{v}{2} & =1 \\\\ u+\\frac{v}{2}-\\frac{v}{2} & =1-\\frac{v}{2} \\\\ u+0 & =1-\\frac{v}{2} \\\\ u & =1-\\frac{v}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
